  "description": "With just a few technical tricks, this thick and flavorful chana masala comes together in an impossibly short time.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: finely minced → grated garlic; cayenne pepper → red chile flakes; Kosher salt → sea salt\n\nNotes: I've added the ginger and garlic to the cold pan with the butter as it melts on purpose: If you are using frozen cubes and add them directly to a heated pan, the temperature difference will cause excess spluttering. Heating the finely minced or grated ginger and garlic from cold also cooks them gently, reducing the chances of burning.",
